Subject: Alias the pyOpenSSL example import so pip can rewrite it
Origin: vendor, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pypa/pip/b3b696fe2122f2339d782517559bfade2cb6b879/tools/vendoring/patches/urllib3.patch
Base-Tree: tarball https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/source/u/urllib3/urllib3-2.8.0.tar.gz sha256:63bf2ead4c879426ebf22ef2a781eeb4aa3b4ae798a0435506f8687fd5bb9b63 path=src/urllib3
Adaptation: Rebased pip's vendoring alias onto the urllib3 2.8.0 wheel. The cited hunk's blank context line had no leading space, so GNU patch applied it only with fuzz and wrote a backup. This hunk keeps that same alias and restores the wheel's blank context lines so the hunk matches exactly. Diff paths stay under src/pip/_vendor so patch -p4 still lands on the copied tree.
Drop-When: never: pip 26.2.2 still vendors urllib3 and this import alias is required whenever a newer urllib3 is copied into that tree

GNU patch treats a blank context line that lost its leading space as fuzz and then writes a backup of the unpatched file. This hunk matches the 2.8.0 wheel, so that backup is not created.

diff --git a/src/pip/_vendor/urllib3/contrib/pyopenssl.py b/src/pip/_vendor/urllib3/contrib/pyopenssl.py
--- a/src/pip/_vendor/urllib3/contrib/pyopenssl.py
+++ b/src/pip/_vendor/urllib3/contrib/pyopenssl.py
@@ -28,8 +28,8 @@
 .. code-block:: python
 
     try:
-        import urllib3.contrib.pyopenssl
-        urllib3.contrib.pyopenssl.inject_into_urllib3()
+        import urllib3.contrib.pyopenssl as pyopenssl
+        pyopenssl.inject_into_urllib3()
     except ImportError:
         pass
 
